  "description": "AHAGEW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C16 H68 Cl2 N16 O23 Tb6 6+,6(Cl1 1-),9(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.496-5.170 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.74-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb6(μ6-O)(μ3-OH)8Cl2(L)4(H2O)14]Cl6·9H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ6-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 14 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
